L222: # SAM 3D
L223: 
L224: SAM 3D Body is one part of SAM 3D, a pair of models for object and human mesh reconstruction. If you’re looking for SAM 3D Objects, cite95†click here .
L225: # SAM 3D Body: Robust Full-Body Human Mesh Recovery
L226: cite96†Xitong Yang†scholar.google.com *, cite97†Devansh Kukreja†www.linkedin.com *, cite98†Don Pinkus†www.linkedin.com *, cite99†Anushka Sagar†www.linkedin.com , cite100†Taosha Fan†scholar.google.com , cite101†Jinhyung Park†jindapark.github.io ⚬, cite102†Soyong Shin†yohanshin.github.io ⚬, cite103†Jinkun Cao†www.jinkuncao.com , cite104†Jiawei Liu†jia-wei-liu.github.io , cite105†Nicolas Ugrinovic†www.iri.upc.edu , cite106†Matt Feiszli†scholar.google.com †, cite107†Jitendra Malik†people.eecs.berkeley.edu †, cite108†Piotr Dollar†pdollar.github.io †, cite109†Kris Kitani†kriskitani.github.io †
L227: Meta Superintelligence Labs
L228: 
L229: *Core Contributor, ⚬Intern, †Project Lead
L230: SAM 3D Body (3DB) is a promptable model for single-image full-body 3D human mesh recovery (HMR). Our method demonstrates state-of-the-art performance, with strong generalization and consistent accuracy in diverse in-the-wild conditions. 3DB estimates the human pose of the body, feet, and hands based on the cite110†Momentum Human Rig (MHR), a new parametric mesh representation that decouples skeletal structure and surface shape for improved accuracy and interpretability.
L231: 3DB employs an encoder-decoder architecture and supports auxiliary prompts, including 2D keypoints and masks, enabling user-guided inference similar to the SAM family of models. Our model is trained on high-quality annotations from a multi-stage annotation pipeline using differentiable optimization, multi-view geometry, dense keypoint detection, and a data engine to collect and annotated data covering both common and rare poses across a wide range of viewpoints.
L232: ## Qualitative Results
L233: 
L234: Input  | SAM 3D Body  | CameraHMR  | NLF  | HMR2.0b
L235: --- | --- | --- | --- | ---
L236:  |  |  |  |
L237:  |  |  |  |
L238:  |  |  |  |
L239:  |  |  |  |
L240: 
L241: Our SAM 3D Body demonstrates superior reconstruction quality with more accurate pose estimation, better shape recovery, and improved handling of occlusions and challenging viewpoints compared to existing approaches.
L242: 
L243: ## Latest updates
L244: 
L245: 11/19/2025 -- Checkpoints Launched, Dataset Released, Web Demo and Paper are out!
L246: ## Installation
L247: 
L248: See cite90†INSTALL.md for instructions for python environment setup and model checkpoint access.
L249: ## Getting Started
L250: 
L251: 3DB can reconstruct 3D full-body human mesh from a single image, optionally with keypoint/mask prompts and/or hand refinement from the hand decoder.
L252: For a quick start, run our demo script for model inference and visualization with models from cite111†Hugging Face†huggingface.co (please make sure to follow cite90†INSTALL.md to request access to our checkpoints.).
L253: 
L254:     # Download assets from HuggingFace
L255:     hf download facebook/sam-3d-body-dinov3 --local-dir checkpoints/sam-3d-body-dinov3
L256: 
L257:     # Run demo script with default ViTdet detector and MoGe2 FOV model
L258:     python demo.py \
L259:         --image_folder <path_to_images> \
L260:         --output_folder <path_to_output> \
L261:         --checkpoint_path ./checkpoints/sam-3d-body-dinov3/model.ckpt \
L262:         --mhr_path ./checkpoints/sam-3d-body-dinov3/assets/mhr_model.pt
L263: 
L264:     # To use SAM3 as the detector to align with online playground of SAM3D
L265:     python demo.py \
L266:         --image_folder <path_to_images> \
L267:         --output_folder <path_to_output> \
L268:         --checkpoint_path ./checkpoints/sam-3d-body-dinov3/model.ckpt \
L269:         --mhr_path ./checkpoints/sam-3d-body-dinov3/assets/mhr_model.pt \
L270:         --detector_name sam3
L271: You can also try the following lines of code with models loaded directly from cite111†Hugging Face†huggingface.co L272: 
L273:     import cv2
L274:     import numpy as np
L275:     from notebook.utils import setup_sam_3d_body
L276:     from tools.vis_utils import visualize_sample_together
L277: 
L278:     # Set up the estimator
L279:     estimator = setup_sam_3d_body(hf_repo_id="facebook/sam-3d-body-dinov3")
L280: 
L281:     # Load and process image
L282:     img_bgr = cv2.imread("path/to/image.jpg")
L283:     outputs = estimator.process_one_image(cv2.cvtColor(img_bgr, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))
L284: 
L285:     # Visualize and save results
L286:     rend_img = visualize_sample_together(img_bgr, outputs, estimator.faces)
L287:     cv2.imwrite("output.jpg", rend_img.astype(np.uint8))
L288: For a complete demo with visualization, see cite112†notebook/demo_human.ipynb .
L289: ## Model Description
L290: ### SAM 3D Body checkpoints
L291: 
L292: The table below shows the performance of SAM 3D Body checkpoints released on 11/19/2025.
L293: Backbone (size)  | 3DPW (MPJPE)  | EMDB (MPJPE)  | RICH (PVE)  | COCO (PCK@.05)  | LSPET (PCK@.05)  | Freihand (PA-MPJPE)
L294: --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---
L295: DINOv3-H+ (840M)
L296: (cite113†config†huggingface.co , cite114†checkpoint†huggingface.co )  | 54.8  | 61.7  | 60.3  | 86.5  | 68.0  | 5.5
L297: ViT-H (631M)
L298: (cite115†config†huggingface.co , cite116†checkpoint†huggingface.co )  | 54.8  | 62.9  | 61.7  | 86.8  | 68.9  | 5.5
L299: ## SAM 3D Body Dataset
L300: 
L301: The SAM 3D Body data is released on cite117†Hugging Face†huggingface.co . Please follow the cite118†instructions to download and process the data.
L302: ## SAM 3D Objects
L303: 
L304: cite95†SAM 3D Objects is a foundation model that reconstructs full 3D shape geometry, texture, and layout from a single image.
L305: 
L306: As a way to combine the strengths of both SAM 3D Objects and SAM 3D Body, we provide an example notebook that demonstrates how to combine the results of both models such that they are aligned in the same frame of reference. Check it out cite119†here .
L307: 
